I spoke with Richard Henderson yesterday at lunch and he strongly
encouraged us to try out a top-of-tree gcc-3.1 and top-of-tree binutils.
Apparently they have implemented support between gcc-3.1 and binutils for
more efficient data layout and relocation types that can make a big
difference at runtime.  He specifically asked because they ran into a few
corner cases that broke on the linux kernel and they'd like us to give it
a whirl as well so that we can try and shake out any remaining problems before
it hits release.  We may need to add a few more (simple) relocation types
to the alpha elf kld relocator if we dont implement them all yet.

